# image-size is pulled in by @docusaurus/mdx-loader, which measures the images a Markdown page references while
# the site is generated. Every published version of image-size is affected and there is no fixed release yet, so
# the finding cannot be resolved by an upgrade.
#
# Not exploitable here: the loop happens inside the site generator, which the doc service runs as a child process
# under a hard timeout (jeap.doc.build.timeout). A crafted image can therefore only make one site's build time out
# - the build is recorded as FAILED, the previously published site stays live, and the service itself is not
# affected. Content only reaches the generator from a system authenticated for its own documentation.
#
# The entries expire, so that this is rechecked rather than left standing: after the date below Trivy reports
# the findings again and the build fails until either a fixed image-size exists or the date is moved on
# deliberately. Last checked 2026-08-27: image-size 2.0.2 is still the newest release and every version is
# affected.
CVE-2025-71329 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2025-71330 exp:2026-11-30
